Relay patch 0001: manual termio backend (pty-less surfaces).

Adds a termio backend that runs no subprocess: the embedder feeds the
program's output (ghostty_surface_write_output), receives what the
terminal writes back and its grid size through callbacks set in
ghostty_surface_config_s (io_mode = GHOSTTY_SURFACE_IO_MANUAL), and
reports the program's end (ghostty_surface_report_exit), which the
surface handles like a child process exiting. Relay uses it to run
terminals over its own SSH client (and, later, on iOS).

Based on the idea of ghostty-org/ghostty#10484 (closed, unmerged), with
input/resize callbacks, exit handling, linefeed-mode translation, and
the threading contract that PR lacked. Applies to the pinned commit in
Scripts/build-libghostty.sh.

